			"Message": "Refactor notification functions to remove unnecessary line breaks\n\n- Removed trailing whitespace in multiple notification function implementations across various files.\n- Ensured consistent formatting for better readability and maintainability.\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "15f8cb994bb9f5bdf774074149d575ffa71f206c"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-04T19:51:03Z",
			"File": [
				"⡿⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1731,
				292
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Finalize CreateEffectForRequest parameter borrowing and standardize blank lines\n\nComplete the parameter borrowing transition in CreateEffectForRequest by adding deferred `Parameters.clone()` calls inside `effect!` macro closures for FileSystem, Languages, StatusBar, TreeView, UserInterface, Webview, WindowUI, and Workspace handlers. Extract derived fields up front in LanguageFeatures provider registration using `_need` intermediates to avoid borrow checker conflicts.\n\nApply blank line formatting across Air stubs, ApplicationState, Binary TLS/runtime build, IPC subsystems (Connection, Encryption, Enhanced, Message, Permission, Security, WindAirCommands, WindServiceHandlers), RPC services, Telemetry, Track, Update, Vine, and Workspace modules. Insert blank lines after struct/enum openings, between fields, after imports, before functions, and inside multi-argument `dev_log!` macro calls.\n\nThis eliminates the last unconditional clones on the hot dispatch path while improving scanability across the entire Mountain source tree.",
			"SHA": "c92357fc7d40a9c97669ad8bbb2f177fafdfbe70"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-06-04T19:46:26Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				1731,
				14
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Mountain): Remove redundant module docs and finalize CreateEffectForRequest parameter borrowing\n\nStrip the remaining module-level rustdoc comments from all CreateEffectForRequest handlers — their table-based documentation duplicated the central dispatcher's meta-module doc and is now superseded by explicit `Matches` predicates in each file.\n\nTighten `Git.Matches` from `starts_with(\"$gitExec\")` to exact equality since only the literal command string is valid. Complete the `&Value` borrowing transition in `LanguageFeatures.CreateProviderEffect` and `Workspace.CreateEffect` by extracting derived fields up front and cloning only inside the macro invocations where ownership is still required.\n\nThis removes dead comments and eliminates the last unconditional clone on the hot dispatch path across all CreateEffectForRequest layers.",
			"SHA": "28e05322406c9829f820dd34e0955e8ffc64c3de"
		}
	],
